        "title": "Nepravidelná slovesa",
        "text": "Mnoho častých sloves nemá v minulém čase -ed. Jejich tvar se musíte naučit zpaměti: go → went, have → had, see → saw, come → came, buy → bought, make → made, take → took, eat → ate, drink → drank. Dobrá zpráva: tvar se nemění podle osoby. Česky šel, šla, šli, anglicky vždy went: I went, she went, we went. A went znamená šel i jel: We went to Prague by train.",
        "examples": [
          { "target": "We went to Prague by train.", "native": "Jeli jsme vlakem do Prahy." },
          { "target": "She bought a red bag.", "native": "Koupila si červenou tašku." },
          { "target": "They came home at ten.", "native": "Přišli domů v deset." },
          { "target": "We had fish and potatoes.", "native": "Měli jsme rybu a brambory." }
        ],
        "reviewed": false
      },
      "words": [
        { "id": "u11-l2-w1", "target": "went", "native": "šel jsem; šla jsem", "note": "Od go. Také jel jsem, jela jsem. Stejné pro všechny osoby.", "reviewed": false },
